# Gap 8's own repro (module-level val initialized by a FUNCTION CALL reads
# 0 under JIT), added to the harness as its own manifestation now that it
# has been unified with gap 9/10's read-side defect (doc/08_tracking/bug/
# jit_run_file_pipeline_gaps_2026-07-30.md section 9): the initializer
# (get_value()) never actually stores its result (42) into X's slot --
# a SEPARATE, write-side defect specific to function-call initializers --
# leaving the slot at its default raw 0. That raw 0 then goes through the
# SAME universal read-side tag-dispatch-on-raw-bits misinterpretation as
# module_global_direct_read_untagged.spl and cross_module_global_import/,
# which is why it prints as "0" (low 3 bits 000 = INT tag, unboxed
# 0>>3=0) rather than some other garbled value. SIMPLE_JIT_STRICT does not
# catch it.
# Expected (interpreter, correct): X=42
fn get_value() -> i64:
    42

val X = get_value()

fn main():
    print("X={X}")
